# hugmesh-sunshine-firewall — thin-desktop nftables-fence convergence timer (60s).
#
# The TIMER half of the Sunshine mesh fence (the OpenRC oneshot renders + loads
# the hugmesh_thin_desktop table once at boot; this cron re-runs it every 60s
# so a hand-flushed table or a late-created tailscale iface converges without a
# reboot). cronie reads /etc/cron.d — the same mechanism every other hugmesh
# reconcile timer uses. STAGED like the vpn/tor crons: this file only lands in
# /etc/cron.d on images built --with-sunshine.
#
# The reconcile is idempotent + FAIL-CLOSED: a render/apply error leaves the
# existing ruleset in place, REMOVES the fence-ready marker
# (/run/hugmesh-sunshine-fence.state) so hugmesh-sunshine-session refuses to
# launch Sunshine, and exits non-zero into this log (stdout+stderr are captured
# here, so cron never mails root).
#
# Field order: min hour dom month dow user command
* * * * * root /usr/sbin/hugmesh-sunshine-firewall >> /var/log/hugmesh-sunshine-firewall.log 2>&1
